# npm blocks package install scripts by default. These genuinely need
# theirs to work, so they're allowed explicitly rather than with a blanket
# opt-out — a new dependency asking for script access will still be blocked
# and surfaced for review.
#
#   prisma           downloads the query engine
#   @prisma/engines  downloads the query engine
#   @prisma/client   generates the typed client from schema.prisma
#   esbuild          installs its platform binary (used by tsx)
#   @nestjs/core     prints a funding message (harmless, but scripted)
allow-scripts=prisma,@prisma/engines,@prisma/client,esbuild,@nestjs/core
